<task id="015" project="spaarke-intake-pipeline-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>FR-09: NDA harness — edit plan → engine → redline/external/clean + clause table → check_outputs → sprk_document + sprk_analysis on the run; pinned standard version stamped; prior markup preserved</title>
    <phase>1 Pipeline core and first doors</phase>
    <gate>blocked — tasks 014, 004, 008 (Clean-copy resolution recorded by the owner 2026-11-26)</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>New BFF harness (.cs) writing documents and analyses on the persist path; depends on 3 tasks; high-risk item R1 in the plan.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>FULL rigor with 3 dependencies and plan Risk Register R1 (prior markup / Clean copy); the first concrete harness defines how every later harness persists.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>P1-E</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>014, 004, 008</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, ai, worker, unit-test, integration-test</tags>
    <estimated-effort>8-10 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Implement the NDA harness on the task 012 contract: build the edit plan through `IAgreementAi` (task 004), run the engine through the task 014 dispatcher, and on a passing `check_outputs` persist the redline, external and (per the 008 resolution) clean outputs plus the clause table as `sprk_document`s on the request and the results as `sprk_analysis`/`sprk_analysisoutput` linked to the run, in one persist step, stamping the pinned NDA standard version on the run and every output. Prior tracked changes and comments in the submitted draft are preserved.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in the BFF write path (sprk_document via SPE, sprk_analysis persistence), AI facades and the intake harness contract. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>
  <goal>`Services/Intake/Harnesses/Nda/NdaIntakeHarness.cs` registered with key `nda` (one DI line; the Binding row exists from task 012), with Analyse = edit plan (persisted before Build), Build = engine dispatch/await via 014, Persist = SPE upload + `sprk_document` + `sprk_analysis`/`sprk_analysisoutput` in one Dataverse transaction with deterministic ids, approval-required = true, a return payload of document ids; tests on the synthetic corpus for clean NDA, counterparty-markup NDA, check failure and version stamp.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Spec FR-09 (acceptance a–f), NFR-09 (pinned "Spaarke NDA – Mutual" v1.2), NFR-10, Unresolved Q1 (resolved 2026-11-26: Clean accepts all revisions from all sides) and Q2 (ADR-049 scope, Path C, confirm in `/adr-check`); project CLAUDE.md §2 (prior markup preserved; redline/external lose no edit and never auto-accept; refused edits "A with B as backup"). On master the engine refuses the WHOLE plan (exit 3) when one edit cannot be placed, and task 001 reports that as `plan_does_not_fit` with the refused edit index + reason code; the harness repairs that edit once through IAgreementAi and re-dispatches, then turns a still-refused edit into a comment plus a "manual" clause-table row; with the accelerator skip-and-report mode (asked 2026-11-26) the engine reports refused edits itself. The harness must not post-process the .docx. The Phase 0 spike report (`notes/spikes/phase0-spike-report.md`, task 008) records the Clean-copy behaviour and the owner's resolution. Classification is already persisted by the orchestrator's Classify stage (task 013); the harness reuses it and never re-classifies. Corpus: `src/accelerators/practices/nda/evals/corpus/nda-01` (clean), `nda-02` (counterparty markup), `nda-03` (injection), `msa-01` (non-NDA).</background>
