  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-007">Scope: every output file. Uploaded to SPE only through `SpeFileStore`; outputs are never served from the staging container.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-013">Scope: AI calls in the harness. Only through `IAgreementAi` (no direct IActionRunner); the classification result is read from the run, not recomputed.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-039">Scope: AI used by the harness. Catalogued Actions only (`agreement-classify`, `agreement-edit-plan`), resolved by ConsumerTypes key.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-049">Scope: output authoring. Outputs are new documents produced by the engine, never authored through Compose or ComposeShadowPatchEngine; no fuzzy text search or .docx post-processing in this harness (Path C; confirm in `/adr-check`, Unresolved Q2).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-002">Scope: Persist. Documents and analyses are created by the BFF write path in one transaction with deterministic ids, so a redelivered Persist creates nothing new (FR-07b).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: prior markup. Existing tracked changes and comments are never accepted, rejected or removed; refused/crossing edits get one AI rewrite, then appear as a comment plus a "manual" clause-table row (FR-09f); the redline and external outputs lose no edit and accept none; the Clean copy accepts all revisions from all sides (FR-09e, owner 2026-11-26).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: version stamping. The pinned standard name and version (v1.2) are written on the run and on every output record (NFR-09).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: tests and fixtures. Synthetic corpus only; never `answer-key/` or a real NDA (NFR-10). No edits under `Services/Finance/Submission/`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-015">Scope: logs and run fields. Ids, outcome codes and counts only; no clause text.</constraint>
    <constraint source="bff-extensions">Scope: the PR. State the Placement Justification, measure the publish-size delta against a fresh master build, ≤ 60 MB total, no new package and no new HIGH CVE.</constraint>
  </constraints>

