  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Read the 008 spike report and notes/decisions.md rows of 2026-11-26 (Clean copy; refused edits "A with B as backup").</step>
    <step order="2">Analyse: call BuildEditPlanAsync; persist the plan reference on the run (blob/staging id, not content) before advancing.</step>
    <step order="3">Build: dispatch via IntakeEngineDispatcher and await completion through the run state (014).</step>
    <step order="4">Persist: on check pass, upload outputs to the request's SPE container via SpeFileStore and create `sprk_document`s + `sprk_analysis`/`sprk_analysisoutput` (clause table) in one transaction with deterministic ids; stamp the standard version; on check failure hold with admin attention.</step>
    <step order="5">Return result: approval-required = true; return payload = document ids.</step>
    <step order="6">Register the harness (key `nda`); write NdaIntakeHarnessTests: nda-01 three outputs + clause table; nda-02 keeps every prior revision/comment and lists refused edits as manual rows; check failure → held, nothing for approval; version stamp; redelivered Persist creates nothing new.</step>
    <step order="7">Run `/adr-check` on the change and record the ADR-049 scope confirmation (Unresolved Q2).</step>
    <step order="8">`dotnet build`, `dotnet test`; measure publish size vs fresh master.</step>
    <step order="9">Update TASK-INDEX.md: change this task's status cell to `✅ [done]`.</step>
    <step order="10">Record deviations in `projects/spaarke-intake-pipeline-r1/notes/`.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the redline or external output loses or accepts any prior or new edit, STOP and escalate (owner rule 2026-11-26); do not post-process the .docx to hide it.</trigger>
    <trigger>If `/adr-check` does not confirm ADR-049 I-5/I-7 are Compose-scoped (Unresolved Q2), STOP and raise the 🔔 ADR Conflict per root CLAUDE.md §6.5.</trigger>
    <trigger>If preserving prior markup would need harness-side .docx edits (beyond what the engine outputs), STOP and coordinate with the accelerator session "acclerator-r1"; never edit the engines.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>reuse-scan.md row 1 (orchestration; invoice-typed, not reusable) and row 14 (app-only AI via facade); spec §11 "Harness contract and registry" (the NDA harness is its first implementation). Persistence reuses SpeFileStore (CAPABILITY-INDEX row 13) and AnalysisResultPersistence.</existing>
    <extension>No — no existing component turns an agreement into engine-produced redline outputs; the harness composes existing writers rather than duplicating them.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>A submitted NDA never produces a marked-up output for attorney approval; success criterion 4 and FR-09 fail.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build and test</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Intake/Harnesses/Nda/NdaIntakeHarness.cs</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/JobProcessingModule.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/seam/Intake/NdaIntakeHarnessSeamTests.cs</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given synthetic nda-01, the harness produces the outputs required by the Clean-copy resolution plus a clause table, `check_outputs` passes, and they are persisted as `sprk_document`s on the request with `sprk_analysis` linked to the run (FR-09a).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given synthetic nda-02 (counterparty revisions and comments), every prior revision and comment remains in the redline and external outputs, and each refused edit appears as a comment plus a "manual" clause-table row (FR-09b).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a `check_outputs` failure holds the run with admin attention and nothing is sent for approval (FR-09c).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The run and every output record carry the pinned standard version v1.2 (FR-09d, NFR-09).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The Clean output accepts all revisions from all sides; the redline and external outputs keep every prior and new edit and accept none (FR-09e, owner 2026-11-26).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Refused edits (FR-09f, owner "A with B as backup"): given a plan with one unplaceable edit, the harness gives that edit one AI rewrite and one more engine pass; if still refused it becomes a comment plus a "manual" clause-table row and the other edits are applied; with the accelerator skip-and-report mode available the harness uses it instead of whole-plan refusal. Negative: the run never fails because of a single refused edit, and no clause text from engine errors is logged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a redelivered Persist creates no second document or analysis; resume after Analyse does not call BuildEditPlanAsync again.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`/adr-check` records the ADR-049 Path C confirmation; no Compose code is referenced.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No test reads `answer-key/` or a real NDA; PR states Placement Justification and publish-size delta (≤ 60 MB, no new HIGH CVE).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named above. Anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in task notes. All tests pass.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Seeding proof requested for the prior-markup preservation test (losing a counterparty revision is a data-loss outcome): feed an output with one prior revision removed, confirm the test fails, restore. If OfficeDocumentPersistence is not the right app-only document writer, use the CAPABILITY-INDEX row 4 write-path owner and record the choice. Accelerator skip-and-report contract (proposed 2026-11-26, PR pending; full text in notes/001-engine-container.md): ooxml_redline.py --skip-unplaceable REPORT.json (codes only, 0-based edit index, closed code set), summary_table.py/check_outputs.py --refused REPORT.json. Accelerator flag, agreed: in skip mode the EXTERNAL redline silently lacks the refused changes, so when refused &gt; 0 the run and the approval Work Item must carry the refused count and the "Changes to make by hand" list so the attorney sees it before approving the external copy. B repair: re-plan only the refused edits through IAgreementAi, one more engine pass on the original draft, then by-hand rows. Deterministic anchoring (owner 2026-11-26, notes/decisions.md): segment_clauses runs first (engine job `segment` operation); the edit-plan AI picks `para` only from the closed para_key list and quotes verbatim; the BFF exact-match pre-check refuses bad anchors (closed codes) before the engine; never fuzzy, approximate or whole-document text matching. Refused edits from the pre-check and from the engine take the same B path (one rewrite, then manual row).</notes>

